-- title:
--   The section ideal in any local frame
-- statement:
--   For a finite family $s$ of sections of $M$ with iso-opens covering $X$, coefficients $v$, and an affine open $U$ with a trivialization $e$ of $M$ on $U$, the ideal of `sectionIdeal k s hs v` on $U$ is generated by the coefficient, in the frame $e$, of $\sum_j k(v_j)s_j$.
--
--   **Notation.** The iso-open of $s$ (`SectionOpens.isoOpen s`) is the union of the opens on which the morphism $s$ restricts to an isomorphism. `sectionIdeal k s hs v` is the comap along `sectionsMorphism` of the ideal sheaf of the hyperplane with coefficients $v$; `sectionCombination k s v` is $\sum_j k(v_j)s_j$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from OpenAI's Lean development, with `Definitions` files of this development imported in place of the upstream modules; these are supporting code for the statement.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (paper: preprints/Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026/main.pdf; Lean: lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri, Apache License 2.0); Lean declaration `OAI.MaximalSeshadri.Projective.sectionIdeal_on_any_frame`, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/AlgebraicGeometry/Seshadri/Divisors/PrincipalSectionIdeal.lean#L84

